ably  diana however passes with flying colors  in the history of balmoral no one has  ever passed a test with such  flying colours even princess anne says  to charles that it's written in the  stars that they be together she did  after all help phillip catch that  elusive stag and it's philip who drives  home charles's duty to marry  made the family position painfully clear  they want me to marry her so we can see  this fairy tale is far from ideal  a young woman in love with a man who's  in love with another woman  in fact this fairy tale reference is  articulated by princess anne later in  episode 9.  once upon a time there was a beautiful  young girl who fell madly in love with a  henson prince  unfortunately the prince was already in  love with someone else who was herself  in love with someone else and they all  lived unhappily ever after charles  himself cries on the evening of his  wedding  juxtaposed to the celebratory fireworks  in the background  although unsubstantiated it is said that  charles told diana the day before the  wedding he was not in love with her  she thought about leaving but went ahead  with the wedding anyway  the real disintegration of the marriage  begins when diana finds out about  charles's love for camilla during a  lunch date with her diana finds out how  much camilla knows about  charles and how little she does they  have fun nicknames for each other fred  and gladys which she'll eventually find  custom designed bracelets charles made  for camilla  they talk every day on the phone while  she can't even get a hold of him it's  not until their tour of australia  everything comes out for once the two  are brutally honest with each other so  much so that they actually patch things  up and things seem to get back on track  even charles decides not to pick up his  calls from camilla but that is  short-lived as diana takes the spotlight  on their trip  he begins to resent her for the  attention she receives while he is  mocked and made a 